# Registers GoogleOAuth2EnvironmentPostProcessor.
#
# This has to be spring.factories. Until 2026-09-06 the registration lived in
# META-INF/spring/org.springframework.boot.env.EnvironmentPostProcessor.imports,
# which looks right and does nothing: the "<fully-qualified-name>.imports" form
# is read for AutoConfiguration only, and Spring Boot loads
# EnvironmentPostProcessor implementations through spring.factories - as its own
# spring-boot jar does for ConfigDataEnvironmentPostProcessor and the rest. The
# post-processor was therefore never invoked anywhere: not under compose, not
# from the jar, not in the test suite. Google sign-in could not work.
org.springframework.boot.env.EnvironmentPostProcessor=\
com.headheartfrees.config.GoogleOAuth2EnvironmentPostProcessor
